ass="documentation-sidebar__item" style="padding-left:16px"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link" href="../javascript/same-height"><span class="documentation-sidebar__link-content"><span>Same height</span></span></a></div></li><li class="documentation-sidebar__list-item"><div class="documentation-sidebar__item" style="padding-left:16px"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link" href="../javascript/toggle"><span class="documentation-sidebar__link-content"><span>Toggle</span></span></a></div></li></ul></li></ul></nav><div class="documentation-sidebar__version"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link" href="../changelog">v<!-- -->3.4.0</a></div></aside><main class="documentation-sidebar__content"><h1 class="bold" id="ordering-utilities"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="ordering#ordering-utilities">Ordering utilities</a></h1>
<p>Use ordering utility classes to control the <em>visual order</em> of flex/grid items responsively. These classes set the CSS <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">order</span></span></code></span> property for a given breakpoint, allowing you to rearrange elements for different screen sizes.</p>
<p>At the moment, only the <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">order</span></span></code></span> values <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">0-2</span></span></code></span> are supported.</p>
