<h2 class="bold" id="responsive-ordering-classes"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="ordering#responsive-ordering-classes">Responsive ordering classes</a></h2>
<p>You can programmatically change the order of elements for specific breakpoints:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>.order-1</code> and <code>.order-2</code> apply <code>order: 1</code>
and <code>order: 2</code> by default (for the smallest breakpoint <b>xs</b>
and up).</li>
<li><code>.order-1-[breakpoint]</code> and <code>.order-2-[breakpoint]</code>
apply the order for the specified breakpoint and up (e.g.,
<code>.order-1-md</code> applies from <b>md</b> and larger).</li>
<li><code>.order-1-[breakpoint]-only</code> and
<code>.order-2-[breakpoint]-only</code> apply the order only for the specified
breakpoint (e.g., <code>.order-2-lg-only</code> applies only at <b>lg</b>).</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Note:</b> There are no <code>.order-1-xs</code> or <code>.order-2-xs</code>
classes. For the smallest breakpoint, use <code>.order-1</code> or
<code>.order-2</code> without a suffix.</p>
